      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10d-catfishes-from-africa/synodontis_angelicus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Formerly these forms were regarded as the subspecies Synodontis angelicus zonatus, but today they are considered a colour variant of the species. They are very decorative and should not be missing in Congo biotope aquariums, where they can be kept together with Congo tetras or large barbs.</p>"
